{
  "manufacturer": "Intesis",
  "manufacturer_slug": "intesis",
  "model": "IntesisBox PA-AC-BAC-64 / PA-AC-BAC-128 (Panasonic CZ-CFUNC2 adaptor)",
  "model_slug": "pa-ac-bac-64-128-cz-cfunc2",
  "aliases": [
    "IntesisBox BACnet/IP Panasonic AC",
    "CZ-CFUNC2 BACnet",
    "Panasonic CZ-CFUNC2 BACnet gateway"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet IP gateway (up to 64 or 128 indoor units)",
  "applies_to": "Panasonic commercial air conditioning indoor units reached through a Panasonic CZ-CFUNC2 communication adaptor (two links, up to 64 indoor units each).",
  "summary": "An older IntesisBox BACnet IP server that connects to one Panasonic CZ-CFUNC2 adaptor and publishes gateway-wide commands plus a fixed block of objects for each indoor unit, up to 64 or 128 units depending on model. Indoor unit instances are (unit number x 256) + offset, so unit 1 uses 256-289. Setup is done with the LinkBoxBACnet tool.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 246,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Indoor unit objects are shown for unit 1 only. Instance = (xxx x 256) + offset, xxx = indoor unit number 1-128. Object names start with IUxxx; the description text carries the link, outdoor and indoor address (K-OA-IA).",
    "This older product talks to the CZ-CFUNC2 adaptor. The newer Intesis INBACPAN016O000/064O000/128O000 (P-Link) uses a different object set. The PA-AC-BAC-64/128 names are also used for that newer product, so check the gateway model before mapping.",
    "Occupancy_All instance 23 and Consumption_Reset 34 come from the object-detail pages; the member-objects table prints the instance column one row off.",
    "The setpoint command AOs' property tables mark Present_Value R; they are listed as writable here because they are the setpoint commands. IUxxx_RemoteControl_Lock and IUxxx_Occupancy are printed R; check on site.",
    "Temperature units follow the gateway setting (°C or °F). Consumption units are printed as kilowatts.",
    "Error code states are a long Panasonic code table (A01, C12, E23 ...) in the manual and are not reproduced here."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "IntesisBox BACnet/IP - Panasonic AC User Manual r2.1 (PA-AC-BAC-64/128)",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "r2.1",
    "url": "https://cdn.chipkin.com/assets/uploads/2018/feb/08-02-04-48_intesisbox_pa-ac-bac-64-128_user_manual_en.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "host": "Chipkin Automation Systems"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Connect the IntesisBox to the CZ-CFUNC2 adaptor and the BACnet IP LAN, configure the indoor units in LinkBoxBACnet, then map each unit's _command and _status objects from its (unit x 256) block. Instances 18-29 act on all units at once.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 258",
        "name": "IUxxx_OnOff_command",
        "why": "Start/stop indoor unit"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 260",
        "name": "IUxxx_Mode_command",
        "why": "Mode command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 262",
        "name": "IUxxx_SetPoint_command",
        "why": "Setpoint command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 265",
        "name": "IUxxx_FanSpeed_command",
        "why": "Fan speed command (4 = auto)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 257",
        "name": "IUxxx_OnOff_status",
        "why": "Run status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 261",
        "name": "IUxxx_SetPoint_status",
        "why": "Setpoint in use"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 263",
        "name": "IUxxx_Room_Temperature",
        "why": "Room temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 256",
        "name": "IUxxx_IU_Exist",
        "why": "Unit found on the adaptor"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MI 270",
        "name": "IUxxx_ErrorCode",
        "why": "Fault code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "No enable point is documented. Remote-controller functions can be locked per unit (MV 271) or for all units (MO 22).",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Default device instance 246; device instance, name and IP are set with LinkBoxBACnet.",
      "One IntesisBox integrates one CZ-CFUNC2 adaptor (bought separately from Panasonic), which has two links of up to 30 outdoor and 64 indoor units each."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "OnOff_All, Mode_All, SetPoint_All, FanSpeed_All and the occupancy objects (instances 18-29) act on every indoor unit.",
      "Outputs only use Priority_Array slot 16; slots 1-15 stay NULL.",
      "State_Text cannot be read as a whole array; read one array index at a time."
    ]
  },
